ruleForT -- SEQ 557 (Tony, 2026-11-07): FOr compiled through the rule door. Rows prefixed RF-.

Not run alone: pop.sh builds each row, everything above this stop(); then the row, a statement that must still run, then a sentinel, one
process per arm under an alarm. Arms: interpreted, and compiled (jitterRule(FOr);). Each row reads exit and sentinel on both arms; the pinned
value; compiled = interpreted, stdout and stderr, witnesses aside; the walk line, native 2 handed 16, registered from docs/ruleJitCensus.md
before this ran; and the fired count, because a door that never opened would agree with itself.

RF-7 and RF-8 fire twice in one process: different sources, and backwards then forwards. The native statements are FOr's two ifs, on
LOOPRESTRICt and reversE, and RF-8's second fire reads reversE absent after a fire that read it present.

RF-S, RF-O and RF-R are the refusal arms. RF-S (the statement arm) and RF-R (the restriction arm) are FOr's own and end in a return. RF-O (the
source) is F-147's shape, a real refuse() inside a handed-over statement, so on the compiled arm it reaches the hand-back and the guard adds
its line: the fifth column pins that. Same value and same refusals otherwise; the behaviour is F-146's.

